kind: ab
question: does streaming Hy4-flash's host experts in its prompt walk lift pp4096 on one RTX 5090 by the derived bulk?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096, prose corpus, one RTX 5090 32 GB, the serving defaults - (opt5 - main) / main, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +117..+159
rounds: 2
sd: 1.1 % rig-log 09-25#v41-prefill-s14, two binaries' per-round pp ratios; the effect is two orders above it
condition: BLOOMERY_MODEL=hy_v4_flash just depth-serve bloomery-opt0315:4096 bloomery-opt5:4096 and their :512 arms,
  BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2, the order rotated every round, one fresh server an arm, the file warm in the page cache
decide-in: land R5 into 0.3.15 and re-table Hy4's row from the release sitting
decide-below: read the stream records (streamed per layer, the lane's busy time against the union's) for the wrong term
decide-above: land, then price a wider ring against decode in the refit table
